\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Typical biased viewpoint settings. (a) Viewing angle disparities: 3DGS trained only with aerial-level views struggles to render consistent ground-level perspectives. (b) Discontinuous camera trajectories: unevenly sampled camera paths lead to fragmented scene reconstruction with blurring artifacts in synthesized views. (c) Systematic coverage gaps: missing observations in specific regions leave parts of the scene weakly supervised.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig_1}{{1}{1}{Typical biased viewpoint settings. (a) Viewing angle disparities: 3DGS trained only with aerial-level views struggles to render consistent ground-level perspectives. (b) Discontinuous camera trajectories: unevenly sampled camera paths lead to fragmented scene reconstruction with blurring artifacts in synthesized views. (c) Systematic coverage gaps: missing observations in specific regions leave parts of the scene weakly supervised}{figure.1}{}}
